 "note": "Ruling R1: one pattern for the name of a repository, a blob store, a cleanup policy, a routing rule and an LDAP connection and for the id of a role, the pattern of store add with a bound of 256 characters; a user id may also hold @ and +. A name outside its pattern is refused with 400 at the field that carries it. Each of the six kinds of the first pattern has a name with @ or + that is refused, so that a user id is the only name that takes them. The 13 cases of store_name in testdata/vectors/cli.json are copied for the blob store name. Ruling R2: a create with a name that exists is refused with 409; a save whose body names another name or id than the stored one is refused with 400 at the name field. Names and ids are compared as they are, so Demo-raw is free beside demo-raw; no source says whether case counts, and this is a choice of this package. A key repeat repeats the name that many times. Ruling R2b replaces R2 for the save of an LDAP connection (op ldap-save, under the row R2). The contract of the interface says for PUT /service/rest/v1/security/ldap/{name}: \"save, 204. The body may carry a new name; the page then moves to it\" (docs/ui/API.md at commit 1e6d884 of the interface repository). The id of a connection is its fixed key: a body that names another id than the stored one is refused with 400 at id (code name-changed). A new name follows R1 (400 at name), and a new name that another connection of the snapshot holds is refused with 409 (name-exists). The stored name sent back is no change, and an absent or null id or name is no change. The snapshot holds each name of the key existing as a connection with the id id-<name>; the stored connection is the one named by the key stored. For every other kind R2 stays as it is.",
